{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s),\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s),\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)⟩,\\,0\\le s<\\sqrt{2}\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)\\cdot \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s))\\cdot \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s))\\cdot \\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s))\\cdot \\sqrt{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)\\cdot \\sqrt{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)\\cdot \\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}s)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}s)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)+2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\sqrt{2}s))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34238" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "312ad665b3ccbfe4bd8a973f1bd1eb3c9cf385327c326fa3f1d9426fd7b2a0c5"} {"question" "q-34238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34238" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}){cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "312ad665b3ccbfe4bd8a973f1bd1eb3c9cf385327c326fa3f1d9426fd7b2a0c5"} {"question" "q-34245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-34245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-64680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,t⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-64680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)}^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(3t))+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{(9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}+(-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\sqrt{{9}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡3t+{cos}^{2}⁡3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}\\,}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-64680" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "312ad665b3ccbfe4bd8a973f1bd1eb3c9cf385327c326fa3f1d9426fd7b2a0c5"} {"question" "q-64680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-64680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{10}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-64680" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-83644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩,\\,0\\le s<6\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-83644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3},\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{3}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-83644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "312ad665b3ccbfe4bd8a973f1bd1eb3c9cf385327c326fa3f1d9426fd7b2a0c5"} {"question" "q-83644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-83644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-83644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-131225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-131225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{tan}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-131225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "312ad665b3ccbfe4bd8a973f1bd1eb3c9cf385327c326fa3f1d9426fd7b2a0c5"} {"question" "q-131225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-131225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"} {"question" "q-131225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071737/state.json" "file_sha256" "e876e55a7f1678009f716f8c3cf364d45e8a1aa8da6e6d17865c60a0d030039e"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2579 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
